# Quality backlog (local memory)

When gates return **many issues**, do **not** re-run `verify`, `lint`, or `typecheck` after every fix.

## Cadence (binding)

| When | Action |
|------|--------|
| Start of fix loop | **One** `npm run qualitygate:capture` |
| Steps 1–4 | Fix **one** item → `npm run qualitygate:backlog -- done <id>` → **no rescan** |
| Step 5, 10, 15… | `npm run qualitygate:capture` again |
| Handoff | `npm run qualitygate:file -- <touched>` |

Also: `npm run qualitygate:changed` every **5 completed todos** (not every todo). See `todo-batch-verify.mdc`.

## Local files (`.local/` — gitignored)

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `.local/quality-backlog.md` | Checklist — what to fix next |
| `.local/quality-last-run.json` | Cached scan output |
| `.local/quality-tracker-state.json` | Per-file tracker (`npm run qualitygate:tracker -- --file`) |

```bash
npm run qualitygate:capture              # scan git-changed src (once per loop)
npm run qualitygate:capture -- src/foo.ts   # scan named files
npm run qualitygate:backlog              # show next items
npm run qualitygate:backlog -- done 3    # mark item fixed (id from backlog md)
```

Canonical detail: `.agents/execute/partials/quality-backlog.md` (included in Implement prompt).

## Anti-patterns

- `qualitygate:file` after every single-line edit.
- Re-running full `npm run lint` / `typecheck` in a tight loop.
- Fixing without recording failures in `.local/quality-backlog.md`.
- Re-counting / re-aggregating gate failures when the log already named files and lines — see `fix-from-gate-output.mdc`.
